# gx3 24-step numerical comparison

`ice_in` matches the original Fortran gx3 case: B grid, one day in 24 one-hour
steps, and `advection='remap'`. Inputs come from the sibling `CICE/input`
directory. Output stays inside this case.

The existing Fortran reference is
`../CICE/cice-dirs/runs/gx3_test/restart/iced.2005-01-02-00000.nc` relative to
the CICE-JAX repository root; Fortran does not need to run again.

The B-grid remap path completed all 24 steps and wrote the final restart on
2026-10-28. The successful run log is saved as `cice.runlog`.
The numerical comparison is still pending. Using the CUDA-enabled environment,
run:

1. `cases/gx3_compare/compare_restart.py`

The comparison checks restart date attributes and every variable. It reports
missing fields, shape differences, and cells outside `rtol=1e-6` or
`atol=1e-10`. A passing restart comparison does not establish matching
history or diagnostics and does not test gradients.

If `run.py` fails, send its traceback and the tail of `cice.runlog` before
running `compare_restart.py`.
